        "note": "My larger Lean project, where this proof was written. The pushforward for the Fubini-Study measure first appears there on 2 June 2026 (commit 9d3ab329); the cell statements for vectors with no vanishing coordinate followed the same day (bd31771a, d8cb4b28), and the cell and frequency statements for every unit vector on 11 June 2026 (ea66a092). The case M = 1 was proved on 31 May 2026 (c2d65361). The files at 9d3ab329 and ea66a092 contain no sorry; their dependencies at those dates were not rechecked for this entry. This repository copies the relevant mathematical development from commit d017e3b, with renamed modules and declarations, unused declarations removed, apexLin moved next to replaceMap so that the Challenge and the proof elaborate it the same way, and the comments rewritten. New here: BornVolumeLean/Volume/BornWeight.lean, which states the theorems for every unitarily invariant probability measure; in BornVolumeLean/Volume/BornFrequency.lean, bornCell and the frequency theorem restated in this repository's free coordinates (freq_tendsto_of_iid there is copied with one bound variable renamed); and the controls. csd-lean4 at that commit uses Lean v4.34.0 and Mathlib 5ed2965; the copied code builds unchanged on this repository's Lean v4.35.0-rc3 and Mathlib 5e0c4e5.",
